<title>FRANCE: ADP Paris imports traffic up 1.9pct Jan-Nov 96.</title>
<headline>ADP Paris imports traffic up 1.9pct Jan-Nov 96.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-November 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 475,499 tonnes, an increase of 1.9 percent on the same period in 1995, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>Global January-November 1996 ADP import traffic, by region, with percentage change on January-November 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		 27,897 tonnes  down 10.2pct</p>
<p> European Union	 58,157 tonnes  up   10.0</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	  10,535 tonnes  up    6.5</p>
<p> North Africa	    9,034 tonnes  down 13.0</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa   47,804 tonnes  up    9.3</p>
<p> North America	 165,790 tonnes  up    2.5</p>
<p> French territories   10,893 tonnes  down  6.5</p>
<p> Latin America	  16,956 tonnes  down  5.2</p>
<p> Middle East	    22,373 tonnes  down  3.0</p>
<p> Far East		106,060 tonnes  up    1.6</p>
<p> Total		   475,499 tonnes  up    1.9</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
